  "rules": "TILES. There are {tiles_total} tiles: {count_of_1} 1, {count_of_2} 2s, {count_of_3} 3s, {count_of_4} 4s, {count_of_5} 5s, {count_of_6} 6s and {count_of_7} 7s.\n\nSETUP. The tiles are shuffled into a face-down pile. Each player is dealt {rack_size} tiles to their rack. Each player is told privately the numbers on every OTHER player's rack, but never their own. Each player starts with {starting_score} points. The discard pile starts empty and is public: everyone always sees which tiles are in it. Seat 1 is the active player in round 1, and the active player then rotates in seat order each round.\n\nEACH ROUND:\n1. The round number and the active player are announced.\n2. The active player chooses a question from the menu below and a respondent, who must be one other player. For NUMBER, the active player also names a number k from {k_min} to {k_max}.\n3. The engine computes the answer exactly, counting only the tiles the respondent can see: every rack except the respondent's own, including the active player's rack. The question, the respondent and the answer are announced to everyone.\n   Menu:\n   EVEN: how many even tiles (2, 4, 6) do you see?\n   HIGH: how many tiles numbered {high_min}, 6 or 7 do you see?\n   NUMBER k: how many tiles numbered k do you see?\n   SUM15: how many of the racks you see total {sum_threshold} or more?\n   PAIR: how many of the racks you see hold at least {pair_min_same} tiles of the same number?\n   MISSING: how many of the numbers {number_range_min} to {number_range_max} appear on none of the racks you see?\n4. GUESS POLL. All players answer at the same moment, without seeing each other's answers. Each either answers PASS or names three numbers (order irrelevant) as a guess at their own rack.\n5. SCORING. A guess that matches your rack exactly as a set of three numbers, duplicates included, scores {correct_guess_points} point. Any other guess scores {wrong_guess_points} point. PASS scores {pass_points} and you keep your rack. Scores may be negative.\n6. REVEAL AND REPLACE. Every player who guessed, right or wrong, has their three tiles announced to all and moved to the discard pile. If the face-down pile then holds fewer tiles than are needed, the discard pile is shuffled into it. Each player who guessed is then dealt 3 new tiles. A player who passed keeps their rack.\n7. Every player is privately told the current racks of all OTHER players.\n8. END CHECK. If any player has {win_points} or more points, the game ends. Otherwise, if the final round (round {final_round}: {final_round_3_players} with 3 players, {final_round_4_players} with 4) has been played, the game ends. Otherwise a new round begins.\n\nThere is no talk; the engine-answered questions are the only shared information.\n\nWINNING. When the game ends, the player with the highest score wins. If two or more players share the top score, it is a draw shared by them."
